# Login Fix Verification

I have fixed the issue where the admin user creation and login were failing due to missing and mismatched password hashing logic.

## Changes Made
- **Centralized Security Logic**: Moved [get_password_hash](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/utils/security.py#10-12) and [verify_password](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/utils/security.py#7-9) to [backend/utils/security.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/utils/security.py).
- **Fixed User Creation**: Updated [backend/crud/user.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/crud/user.py) to correctly import security functions and accept pre-hashed passwords.
- **Updated Auth Router**: Refactored [backend/routers/auth.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/routers/auth.py) to use the shared security functions.

## Verification Steps

### 1. Rebuild and Start Containers
Run the following command in your terminal to rebuild the backend and start the services:

```powershell
docker-compose down -v
docker-compose up --build
```
> [!NOTE]
> `docker-compose down -v` ensures that the database volume is removed so that [init_admin.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/init_admin.py) runs again to create the admin user.

### 2. Verify Admin Login
1. Open your browser and go to [http://localhost](http://localhost).
2. Try to login with the admin credentials:
   - **Email**: `admin@synapseplan.com`
   - **Password**: [admin](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/init_admin.py#10-46)

### 3. Verify Registration (Optional)
1. Try to register a new user.
2. Verify that you can login with the new user.
